--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
already declared with different type
--
A function template with the return type `auto &&', declared before its
definition, was instantiated twice with the same arguments; the second
instantiation, from the declaration, had the undeduced return type and was
rejected as a conflicting redeclaration of the first.  Only a bare `auto'
was accepted.  The MSVC STL's _Tuple_get, used by std::pair's piecewise
constructor (std::map::emplace), has this shape.
